"""
// functinality SIG Instruction doc
fields (datatypes) with multiple values
timing_sequence (string)
allDays  (string)
seq.rel.when (string)


regimen -> variant > <portion?> -> components/cui -> step_number
step is repeated once or more -> sig anatomy 
(cycle_length_lb, cycle_length_ub, cycle_length_unit, timing_sequence) ->
allDays [-> freq/cui -> 


component_role         component
---------------------------------
locoregional           24
primary systemic      456
secondary systemic    133


class                       component
-------------------------------------
IV continuous canonical Sig       22
IV intermittent canonical Sig    210
Non-IV canonical Sig             320
Non-canonical Sig                233
Rad Sig                            7

------------------------ Sigs Anatomy
{
Sigs types:
    non-repeating ~ course : can have No Upper Bound (NUB) - indefinite
    repeating ~ cyclic : definite
}
* Cycles (or courses) without enumerated values, “One course” is a frequently encountered cycleSIG. 
cycle_length_lb, cycle_length_ub = 1, cycle_length_unit = “indeterminate”
* conditional length = “Continued until CR or 60 days”, which means that the
medication is continued until complete remission and/or 60 days have elapsed.
* for convenience in modeling : Indefinite courses (e.g., a drug taken once per day and continued indefinitely) are
transformed into 28-day cycles
* 12-month courses are transformed into 28-day cycle x 13 cycles
* 2-year courses are transformed into 28-day cycle x 26 cycles
* 3-year courses are transformed into 28-day cycle x 39 cycles
* and so forth for 4-year, 5-year, and so on...


The timing sequence variable specifies the exact cycles in which a given component 
of a regimen is delivered 
------------------------
timing_sequence: timing for course and cycle, specified by exact cycle
timing_sequence = 1 // course, drug taken once
timing_sequence > 1 // sequential courses 
timing_sequence = [\d,\d,\d] // cycles of a regimen // Standard form for repeating (cyclic) regimen
timing_sequence = 0 // pre-phase treatment
timing_sequence = \d,\d,(\d) // a must (optional) // has specified end
timing_sequence = \d,\d,(+n) // a must (optional) // does not have specified end
timing_sequence = 1,(+1) // same as +n
timing_sequence = 1,(+2) // means 1, 3, 5  // skips until indefinite !
// As of May 19, 2025 there are 4208/23832 (18%) rows with the (+1) notation, and 15/23832 (0.06%) with the (+2) notation.
                                    0/  #2024 version...                       15/23551
                                    
timing_sequence = \d, (+c) // until conditional criterion descirbed currently in cyclesigs_notes is met

allDays
----------
Negative days are padded with a caret
Optional days are enumerated with parentheses, e.g., “1,3,(5)”
Indefinite optional extensions are represented by “(+n)”
Conditional endings are represented by “(+c)”; - difficult to model -uncommon

"""


pre_run  cleanings
